{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with pca_n2000/multiprofile/avgpool (config_002) achieves 0.591 acc, the best result so far, while image-only with resnet50 (config_010) is very weak at 0.208. We have no multimodal result yet. Question: Does combining image features with the strong RNA signal via simple concat fusion improve upon the RNA-only baseline? This directly tests whether the image modality contributes useful complementary information or merely adds noise. Why this is the best next experiment: The multimodal-vs-unimodal question has the highest information value under budget constraints—if concat fusion with the best-known RNA setup fails to beat 0.591, it strongly suggests image features (at least from resnet50) are not contributing, allowing us to deprioritize the ~36 multimodal configs and focus remaining budget on RNA encoder selection (scvi, scgpt). If it does help, it confirms fusion is worth exploring and motivates testing weighted fusion and ViT-L image encoder next. Using avgpool (proven best aggregation) and pca_n2000 (proven best encoder so far) isolates the fusion question with minimal confounding."
}

